{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/42690-mummies-of-the-east","id":42690,"title":"Mummies of the East","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T21:42:03-08:00","id":42690,"title":"Mummies of the East","content":"So, in my attempts to design some unusual settings for the mummies to have flashback scenes, I decided on the far east. In attempts to add some flavor and exoticism, thought of exchanginng some words, terms, and ideas for local flavor (especially non-iremite ones). In doing so, i decided to pull some inspiration from Kindred of the East. Not only does the history of the kuei jin fit, but the dharmas could be the decrees. Both games reference soul parts. Does anyone have any ideas on a sort of full on crossover? What Pillars would you say are Yin, Yang, Hun, and P'o?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T23:06:49-08:00","id":42718,"title":"","content":"P'o is definitely Sheut. I would say.... Ren would be Hun, and Ab, Ba, and Ka would be divided between Yin and Yang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T00:26:24-08:00","id":42749,"title":"","content":"You could also make an argument for Sheut being Yin (concerned as it is with the energies and nature of death). The problem here is that both the pillars and the kuei-jin soul-bits are simplifications of very complex, very <i>very</i> different metaphysical systems. They don't map terribly well to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:26:51-08:00","id":42932,"title":"","content":"Actually the Pillars should still work, but call them by their English (well translated) names instead and it fits more cultures.<br /> <br /> Much of Arisen Magic is more Primordial and thus can fit other cultures, rather just Egyptian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:48:08-08:00","id":43216,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Sheut is really the trouble maker, especially while trying to keep a yin-yang duality. It is quite a difficult mash together, as Gabby said. But certainly functional. So far, Ive gotten.. sheut as yin, as it is quiet, dark, necrotic, and mysterious. p'o could be Ab, for the fierce passions and egoism. Hun could be Ka, to represent higher values and meaning. Ba is most likely to be yang, as ba is all about action and doing and little else. And ren, then, would be the balance. I decided to call it Karma (because ren also ties to Fate in mage, and represents ones gathered identity). However, as gabby said, the fit isnt perfect, especially when you add the dharmas into account. Thus far, dharma = decree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}